  "observations": "Root ordered second reading: whole then both supplied halves preceded image-first observations and text opening. All27 fresh audit crops were personally viewed. Every agreed/differing word, accent, punctuation, abbreviation, product, index, prime, arrow, deletion, insertion and underline was compared with the consolidated page. The opening > and the separate lower bar in the limit index are confirmed; the typed index set J in(ii), unaccented Etant, enngroupes, original opératerus letter order, wavy object arrow, doubled T topology symbols and three Exp. cancellations are preserved. At the right edge of the operators line, r and s are both visible in overlapping positions; neither is inferred to be deleted. The first H/prime/font doubt and the cancelled fini/edge-punctuation doubts remain. The altered limit initial now records its visible B-like possibility. A closed o surviving under i in fibré is added to the diplomatic text. The two exchange arrows are reproduced in inline TikZ to preserve word position. Manuscript9 and archival40 remain distinct. No context or mathematical proof check was used."
